  "request": {
    "model": "nomic-embed-text:latest",
    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nThe commercial driver attends after a long shift with a folder containing a current signed letter, older screening paperwork and a handwritten personal account, and the nurse reconstructs the chronology before recording the present findings; differences between the records are described explicitly rather than resolved by treating the newest-looking photocopy as automatically authoritative.\n\nAlthough the driver repeatedly points to a systolic figure of 158 as reassurance, the dated treating-doctor record confirms persistent BP 158/106 mmHg after repeat resting checks, and the nurse separately records the lower and upper pressures; the driver cannot provide the specialist information or demonstrate a four-week period of effective treatment, and his account of an old normal check does not replace today's documented diastolic pattern.\n\nPart of the usual route requires reversing near workers and reading changing signs before entering a customer site, although today's assessment takes place in a quiet room; the driver is asked to describe the sequence and timing of difficulties, and the note preserves the difference between an occupational concern, a suspected mechanism and a completed clinical assessment.\n\nThe record is prepared for the reviewing clinician with the sequence of events and the provenance of the available findings intact, because the employer summary and the driver's account answer different questions; a completed test is retained as such, but an unresolved detail is not filled in from a family member's history or from an earlier document with different testing conditions.\n"
    ],
    "truncate": false
  },
  "provider_called": true,
  "status": "completed",
